            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Why_Shared_Rhythm_Matters.png",
            "icon": "none",
            "icon_width": 48,
            "title": "Why Shared Rhythm Matters",
            "heading_bottom_content": "",
            "content": "<p>Wellbeing is often treated as an individual pursuit.</p><p>But historically, rituals were rarely practiced alone.</p><p>Morning light, shared meals, evening quiet, breath, sound, silence, repetition — these experiences once existed within families, communities, and environments that reinforced rhythm through daily life.</p><p>Modern life has weakened many of these shared signals.</p><p>Mirellis community exists as a quieter response to that fragmentation — a space shaped around shared morning and evening rituals, slower pacing, and intentional return.</p><p>Community here is not built through noise or constant interaction.</p><p>It forms gradually through shared rhythm.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "item_Yk9k3E"
